---
import Layout from '../../studio/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';

const title = 'Terms of Service — PingDeck';
const description = 'Terms of Service for PingDeck (com.yanerapps.pingdeck), a multi-host ping monitor for Android by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="PingDeck navigation" class="product-nav">
      PingDeck <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Terms
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/pingdeck/privacy">Privacy</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/pingdeck/support">Support</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">PingDeck for Android (<code>com.yanerapps.pingdeck</code>)</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Effective: from PingDeck&rsquo;s release on Google Play</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of the PingDeck Android application ("the app"), made by Yaner Yang, publishing
      as Yaner Apps ("we", "us"). By installing or using the app you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use
      the app. How the app handles data is described separately in the <a href="/pingdeck/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> PingDeck sends network probes from your phone to the hosts you choose. Monitor
      only hosts and networks you own or have permission to test; how you use it is your responsibility. Pro is an
      optional one-time purchase, sold and billed by Google Play. The app is provided as is, it is not a guarantee
      that you will learn of every outage, and our liability is limited as far as the law allows.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. What PingDeck does</h2>
    <p>
      PingDeck checks whether the hosts you add are reachable, using ICMP ping, TCP connections and HTTP or HTTPS
      requests, and shows their status, response times and statistics. It can discover devices on a local network
      you choose to scan, alert you when a host goes down or comes back, show a summary in a notification and a
      home screen widget, and, if you set them up, call a webhook or open links built from your own templates. It
      needs Android 12 or later and works without an account.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your responsibility for how you use it</h2>
    <p>
      Monitoring means sending traffic to other systems. You use the app at your own risk, and you alone are
      responsible for how you use it and for what follows from it. In particular:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Only what you may test.</strong> Monitor and scan only hosts and networks you own or have
        permission to test. Probing other people's systems may break their terms, your network provider's or
        employer's rules, or the law where you are.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No harm to others.</strong> Do not use PingDeck to flood, overload or disrupt any system or network,
        to map networks you are not authorised to examine, or for any other unlawful purpose. Choose intervals and
        rates that the hosts and networks you monitor can bear.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your destinations.</strong> Webhooks and custom link commands send host details to addresses you
        enter. You are responsible for choosing them and for what those services do with the data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Costs.</strong> Monitoring uses mobile data and battery. Charges from your carrier or network
        provider are yours.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Monitoring is best effort</h2>
    <p>
      PingDeck reports what your device can see from where it is. A host may look down because of your own
      connection, a firewall or the host's settings, and look up while a service on it is failing. Android, battery
      savers, other apps or a device restart can pause or stop monitoring in the background and delay or block
      alerts. Do not rely on PingDeck alone to monitor systems where a missed or late alert could cause harm or loss.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      PingDeck has no accounts and no servers of ours. Your host list, settings and statistics exist only on your
      device, so we cannot recover them if they are lost, for example when you uninstall the app, clear its data or
      lose the device. Export your host list to keep your own copy. Exported files are not encrypted, so keep them
      somewhere safe.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Licence</h2>
    <p>
      We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the app on
      Android devices you own or control, in line with these terms and the Google Play Terms of Service. PingDeck is
      intended for adults. You may not copy, resell, sublicense or redistribute the app, remove its notices, tamper
      with its purchase checks, or reverse engineer it except where the law expressly allows it. The app, its name,
      icon and design remain ours.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Free version, ads and Pro</h2>
    <p>
      PingDeck is free to download. The free version shows ads from Google AdMob and limits how many hosts are
      monitored at the same time; the status, statistics, history, alerts and exports work in full. Watching an
      optional rewarded ad gives you Pro for a short time. Pro is an optional one-time purchase that removes ads,
      removes the limits and adds extra features. What Pro includes and its price are shown in the app before you
      buy; prices come from Google Play in your local currency and may change over time.
    </p>
    <h3>Buying Pro</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Pro is sold and billed by Google Play and charged to the payment method in your Google account. We never see your payment details.</li>
      <li>Pro is a one-time purchase, not a subscription: there is no recurring charge.</li>
      <li>If your payment is pending, Pro starts once Google Play confirms the payment.</li>
      <li>The app confirms Pro with Google Play. If it cannot reach Google Play, Pro keeps working for a limited time since the last confirmation, after which the app shows the free version until it can check again.</li>
      <li>Pro is tied to the Google account that bought it, not to a device. Use <strong>Restore purchase</strong> in the app's settings after a reinstall or on a new device signed in to the same account.</li>
      <li>When Pro ends, for example after a refund or when a rewarded trial runs out, nothing in your host list or settings is deleted; only Pro features stop being available, and they come back when Pro does.</li>
      <li>
        Refunds are handled by Google Play under its
        <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637" rel="noopener" target="_blank">refund policy</a>.
        If something went wrong with a purchase, write to us as well and we will help where we can. Nothing in these
        terms limits any right of withdrawal or refund that consumer law gives you.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Availability and changes to the app</h2>
    <p>
      We may update, change or remove features, and the app may stop working in part or in full because of changes
      to Android, Google Play, your device or network that we do not control. Pro unlocks the features the app
      offers to Pro users; it does not promise any particular feature forever or updates for any fixed period.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, the app is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy of its measurements,
      non-infringement, or that it will work on any particular device, network or Android version, or without
      interruption or error.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
      punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits, revenue or business, including an outage you were not
      alerted to, arising from your use of or inability to use the app. Our total liability for all claims relating
      to the app is limited to the amount you paid us for the app in the 12 months before the claim, or, if you paid
      nothing, to zero.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited by law, such as
      liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for intent or gross negligence, and
      nothing affects the statutory rights you have as a consumer, including those under the consumer protection
      laws of the EEA and the United Kingdom.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, you agree to cover our costs and losses arising from claims by others that result
      from your breach of these terms or your unlawful use of the app, such as probing systems you were not allowed
      to.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Ending these terms</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using the app at any time by uninstalling it. If you seriously breach these terms, your licence
      ends. Sections 2, 4 and 8 to 12 continue to apply after that.
    </p>

    <h2>12. General</h2>
    <p>
      If a provision of these terms is found invalid, the rest remain in effect. Our not enforcing a provision is not
      a waiver of it. These terms, together with the privacy policy, are the whole agreement between you and us about
      the app. Where the law of your country of residence gives you mandatory consumer protections, they apply in
      addition to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change, the updated version is published on this page with a new date. Material changes will
      also be noted in the app's release notes. Continuing to use the app after a change means you accept the updated
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Yaner Apps &mdash; <a href={mailto('PingDeck terms')}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
